cff-version: 1.2.0
title: malayalam-factcheck-corpus
message: >-
  If you use this corpus or pipeline in academic work, please cite it
  using the metadata below. Please also cite the underlying fact-check
  publishers whose articles your records are derived from (the
  source_id field on each record points to the publisher).
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Hrishikesh
    family-names: Bhaskaran
    email: hello@stultus.in
repository-code: "https://github.com/stultus/malayalam-factcheck-corpus"
url: "https://github.com/stultus/malayalam-factcheck-corpus"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible batch pipeline that ingests Malayalam fact-check
  articles from IFCN-certified Indian portals and produces a
  versioned, deduplicated Parquet corpus of (claim, verdict, evidence)
  triples for training claim-verification and misinformation-detection
  models. Source-attribution and verdict provenance are preserved on
  every record.
keywords:
  - misinformation
  - fact-checking
  - claim-verification
  - malayalam
  - indian-languages
  - low-resource-nlp
  - dataset
license: MIT
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-05-01"
